The first line is the upstream: the die analysis, the ROM transcription and
the filter topologies this synthesizer is built on are Olivier Galibert's work
for MAME, under these terms, and the notice travels with anything derived from
them. The second is Tamas Geczy's work in his votraxsc01 add-on, under these
terms too: the NVDA driver nvda-addon/addon/synthDrivers/votraxNative.py is
derived from his; src/ttv_tables.c carries his transcription of the NRL
phoneme-to-Votrax rules and his exception dictionary; and the rate and cancel
behaviour of the scheduler follow his design. The third is the work done in
this repository on top of that -- the C synthesizer and scheduler, the
matcher, number reader and prosody of the English front end, the changes to
the NVDA driver, the GUI and the tooling. All are under the same terms; see
NOTICE.md for which is which.

